  "term": "spontaneous alternation",
  "definition": "Spontaneous alternation is a maze-based behavioral test, here described with a four-arm maze, in which an animal’s naturally changing choices between maze arms are observed. In this research context, it is used as a learning-related task while measures such as acetylcholine efflux in the medial prefrontal cortex are recorded during performance.",
